# ── A course workspace living in this checkout ────────────────────────────────
# Running `paideia init-course` here (the fastest way to exercise the harness)
# turns the repo root into a course folder. Those are the student's own
# materials — lecture PDFs, homework scans, an error log — and belong to the
# course, never to the package. Keep them out of the repo by default; a file
# genuinely meant for the project can still be added with `git add -f`.
/.course-meta
/AGENTS.md
/opencode.json
/materials/
/converted/
/answers/
/course-index/
/errors/
/quizzes/
/mock/
/twins/
/chain/
/derivations/
/cheatsheet/
/weakmap/
